 order","confidence":0.57,"observed":false,"title":"iPhones & Luxury Perfumes Seen Floating After Cargo Ship Sinks In Strait of Hormuz"}],"revisions":[],"entities":[{"name":"Hormuz","kind":"person","mentions":12},{"name":"Iran","kind":"place","mentions":12},{"name":"Middle East","kind":"place","mentions":11},{"name":"Strait","kind":"place","mentions":11}],"disputes":[],"summary":{"text":"Iran has increased threats to shipping in the Strait of Hormuz, a waterway between the Persian Gulf and the Gulf of Oman. The Strait is about 104 miles long and varies in width from 60 miles to 24 miles. A cargo ship sank in the strait after hitting a mine, with more than 2,500 containers on board. The IRGC, Iran's navy, is responsible for the mine.","text_hi":null,"model":"qwen2.5-1.5b-instruct-q4_k_m.gguf","created_at":"2026-10-15T07:30:06Z"},"context":{"background":[{"title":"Strait of Hormuz","extract":"The Strait of Hormuz is a waterway between the Persian Gulf and the Gulf of Oman. On the north coast lies Iran, and on the south coast lies the Musandam Peninsula under the Musandam Governorate of Oman, with a portion of the southwest of the peninsula under the United Arab Emirates (UAE). The strait is about 104 miles long, with a width varying from about 60 mi to 24 mi.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strait_of_Hormuz","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"places":[{"title":"Iran","extract":"Iran, officially the Islamic Republic of Iran, and historically known as Persia, is a country in West Asia. It borders Iraq to the west; Turkey, Azerbaijan, and Armenia to the northwest; the Caspian Sea to the north, Turkmenistan to the northeast; Afghanistan to the east; Pakistan to the southeast; and the Gulf of Oman and the Persian Gulf to the south. With a population of over 92 million, Iran ranks 17th globally in both geographic size and population. It is divided into five regions with 31 provinces. Tehran is the nation's capital and largest city and serves as its primary economic center.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"IR"},{"title":"Singapore","extract":"Singapore, officially the Republic of Singapore, is an island country in Southeast Asia. Its territory comprises a main island, over 60 satellite islands and islets, and one outlying islet. The country is about one degree of latitude north of the equator, off the southern tip of the Malay Peninsula, bordering the Strait of Malacca to the west, the Singapore Strait to the south along with the Riau Islands in Indonesia, the South China Sea to the east and the Straits of Johor along with the State of Johor in Malaysia to the north.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Singapore","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"SG"}],"arc":{"reports":48,"first_seen":"2026-10-09T18:01:09Z","first_title":"Tanker attacks in Strait of Hormuz surge to wartime high as Iran tries to choke off oil exports","first_url":"https://news.google.?oc=5","first_publisher":"CNBC","earlier":[{"id":"e_8607a65ec1fc","title":"Shafaq News..Iran detects burning tanker near Strait of Hormuz","date":"2026-10-16T12:52:53Z","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMigwFBVV95cUxQZ3JCa1NOS1hkTEdqaVA0WE1hNEMxdjJSeFZRRmdpNXV5cWRNNHZPVTMxTkFDQjRPNHg2VTZsTl9MUE1IalRROU1mT2IzX1lfdUhKRW9TcEI4M2RNd19WUUQtb2ZRX1pGNGZKN0ZkaG45VER6ZE1ERjFFZXh6SFhfcmxISQ?oc=5","publisher":"شفق نيوز","verification":"single_source_report"},{"id":"e_07742c9ba86d","title":"Iranian Army: We Have Full Control of the Strait of Hormuz, Shipping Traffic Remains Extremely Limited","date":"2026-10-16T14:16:17Z","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiUEFVX3lxTE9Rd041bnNZeklTSVczeWNqUHczN0RKelU0aVIyNGFlRXlFaG8xZVFnUzlUcC1wSlFQeVVmenJRNFEyVnU2ZTdTWFBhTm1DODRI?oc=5","publisher":"شبكة يافا الإخبارية","verification":"single_source_report"},{"id":"e_0cbef8d3fd30","title":"Iran says oil tanker hit naval mine in Strait of Hormuz","date":"2026-10-17T03:19:05Z","url":"http://w